Type Use when Sentinel (<code>errors.New(...)</code>) Fixed error without dynamic context <code>*BusinessError</code> Need HTTP status + client message + optional wrapping <pre><code>// Sentinel — no context needed
var ErrContractNotFound = errors.New("contract not found")

// BusinessError — needs HTTP status
return &amp;sharedErr.BusinessError{
    Code:    "CONTRACT_NUMBER_TAKEN",
    Message: fmt.Sprintf("contract number %q is already in use", number),
    Status:  409,
    Err:     pgErr,
}
</code></pre> <p>In the handler, <code>mapError</code> handles both:</p> <pre><code>func (h *contractHandler) mapError(err error) error {
    var bizErr *sharedErr.BusinessError
    if errors.As(err, &amp;bizErr) {
        return c.Status(bizErr.Status).JSON(fiber.Map{
            "error": fiber.Map{
                "code":    bizErr.Code,
                "message": bizErr.Message,
            },
        })
    }
    switch {
    case errors.Is(err, domain.ErrContractNotFound):
        return fiber.NewError(fiber.StatusNotFound, "contract not found")
    // ...
    }
}
</code></pre>

